From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jaime Dias <jaimejosediasnt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 30 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Dump the guest stack when translated code stops

A guest that ends with PC = 0 and A6 = 0 has jumped through a library or
device base that was never filled in -- the classic unchecked
OpenLibrary/OpenDevice. The register dump says that much and no more.
The return address the JSR pushed says which code did it, and it is
sitting at A7.

Demo Reel 3 dies exactly that way on this machine, twice with identical
registers, and there was no way to name the caller from outside.

Guest addresses are directly dereferenceable here and both sides are
big-endian, so a plain load reads the m68k value. Guarded, because a
crashed guest's A7 is not to be trusted.
---
 src/aarch64/start.c | 34 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 34 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/aarch64/start.c b/src/aarch64/start.c
--- a/src/aarch64/start.c
+++ b/src/aarch64/start.c
@@ -2445,8 +2445,40 @@
 
     kprintf("[JIT]\n");
     M68K_PrintContext(&__m68k);
 
+    /*
+     * The stack, because the registers alone do not say who called.
+     *
+     * A guest that ends here with PC = 0 and A6 = 0 has jumped through a
+     * library or device base that was never filled in -- the classic
+     * unchecked OpenLibrary/OpenDevice. The registers say that much and no
+     * more; the return address the JSR pushed says which code did it, and it
+     * is sitting at A7.
+     *
+     * Guest addresses are directly dereferenceable here and both sides are
+     * big-endian, so a plain load reads the m68k value. Guarded because a
+     * crashed guest's A7 is not to be trusted: word-aligned, above the
+     * vector table, below the top of anything this machine maps.
+     */
+    {
+        uint32_t sp = __m68k.A[7].u32;
+
+        if (sp >= 0x1000 && sp < 0x40000000 && (sp & 1) == 0)
+        {
+            const uint32_t *stack = (const uint32_t *)(uintptr_t)sp;
+            int i;
+
+            kprintf("[JIT] Stack at A7 = 0x%08x:\n", sp);
+            for (i = 0; i < 8; i++)
+                kprintf("[JIT]     +%02x: 0x%08x\n", i * 4, stack[i]);
+        }
+        else
+        {
+            kprintf("[JIT] Stack at A7 = 0x%08x not readable\n", sp);
+        }
+    }
+
     M68K_DumpStats();
 
     kprintf("[JIT] Number of m68k instructions executed (rough): %lld\n", __m68k.INSN_COUNT);
     kprintf("[JIT] Number of ARM cpu cycles consumed: %lld\n", cnt2 - cnt1);
